<VI _name="lvai_run_and_read_typed.vi" description="Run a VI and read back EVERY control and indicator value it holds afterwards\2C rendered as XML text - and set its inputs ACCORDING TO EACH CONTROL'S OWN TYPE rather than as strings only.\0A\0AThe predecessor\2C lvai_run_and_read.vi\2C wires the incoming string straight into Ctrl Val.Set\2C whose Value terminal is a Variant. A string variant only matches a STRING control\2C so a path\2C numeric or boolean control could not be set at all - measured repeatedly\2C where five separate agents each worked around it by generating throwaway copies of the VI under test with the values baked into the control defaults.\0A\0AThis helper reads the target's front panel first\2C matches each requested name against the control labels\2C and asks the control what it is through the Class Name property. LabVIEW answers String\2C Path\2C Digital (for every numeric representation\2C DBL and I32 alike)\2C Boolean\2C Array or Cluster - measured 2026-09-16 on one control of each type. The case structure converts the incoming string accordingly and only then calls Ctrl Val.Set.\0A\0AAn ENUM takes an item name or an index\3A the name is looked up in the control's own Strings []\2C anything else is read as a number\2C and text that is neither is sent as a STRING so that Ctrl Val.Set refuses it BEFORE the run instead of setting item 0 in silence. An ARRAY or a CLUSTER takes LabVIEW's own XML for the value wrapped in LvVariant\2C which Unflatten From XML turns into a Variant carrying its type - measured 2026-09-25 on a 2D string array\2C round trip exact. The caller never names the type.\0A\0AA name that matches no control on the target's panel produces an INVALID REFNUM error from the Class Name property rather than LabVIEW's own control-name message\2C because the lookup happens before the set. The error still names the property node and still stops the run before Run VI.\0A\0AInput Names and Input Values are two newline-separated lists\2C paired by position. A LINE BREAK INSIDE A VALUE travels encoded - LF as the control character 0x1E and CR as 0x1D - and is decoded here before the value is converted\2C so a multi-line string or a compound value with a multi-line member arrives intact. The server encodes it\3B the constant named encoded line feed is how the server recognises a helper that decodes. Driven by RunVIAsTopLevel\2C which marshals strings only - which is why every input here is a string and the typing happens inside.">
